`topLevelArgs` returned EMPTY for those two sources. Why? Look at my implementation:

```dart
String topLevelArgs(String args) {
  ...
  for (...) {
    final ch = args[i];
    if (ch == '(') { depth++; continue; }
    if (ch == ') { ... continue; }
    if (depth == 0) out.write(ch);
  }
```

The captured `args` from `balancedArgs` STARTS with the opening `(` of the construction: `(voxelWorld: w, theme: resolve(x))`. So depth becomes 1 immediately, and EVERYTHING is nested → output empty. I treated the construction's own opening paren as a nested group!

Fix: the captured args string always begins with the construction's `(`. Options:
- Skip the first char if it's `(` (the construction's own opener), then strip nested groups.
- Or track depth relative: ignore the FIRST `(` encountered (treat as the frame), strip the rest.

Robust approach: strip a leading `(` (and the matching trailing `) first, then strip nested groups from the interior:

```dart
String topLevelArgs(String args) {
  var s = args;
  if (s.startsWith('(') && s.endsWith(')) {
    s = s.substring(1, s.length - 1);
  }
  final out = StringBuffer();
  var depth = 0;
  for (...) { same as before }
  return out.toString();
}
```

That handles both wrapped rendererConstructionsOf (args include outer parens). For the main-tree path, same shape. Empty args (`''`) → untouched.

Also — the main guard test failed too: same root cause (all sites' args → ''). After the fix, re-run. Also the interpolation pin failed with '' — same cause (nothing to do with the masker necessarily; will confirm after fix).

